  "description": "§7d: two copies of native_sky_falloff.json's own 11x11 roofed room, side by side in one frame, identical in every way except which door def sits in the south wall gap -- room A a plain wood Door (BaseMaxHitPoints 160, the DoorLeakMath reference, so it must leak exactly like pre-§7d), room B Odyssey's AncientBlastDoor (6000, ratio 37.5, decays to effectively opaque). Depth is expected identical between the two (door strength never changes BFS distance, only the flood's strength -- the explicit design constraint this feature shipped under), so a difference in wood_door_depth vs door_strength_depth would itself be a bug. Run WITHOUT Ambient Light, same reason native_sky_falloff.json gives, and forces the Realistic preset first for the same masking reason (Cinematic's MinIndoorBrightness floor dwarfs this term).",
